Zero-migrations mode (pre-1.0)
-------------------------------
Schema is managed by Base.metadata.create_all (session.py: _apply_migrations_sync).
No migration files exist in versions/.  The Alembic scaffolding (env.py,
alembic.ini, script.py.mako) is kept wired so migrations can resume without
structural changes.

Runbook to resume migrations:
1. alembic revision --autogenerate -m "baseline"
2. Review and trim the generated file (remove noise for existing tables).
3. alembic stamp <revision>  — stamp existing create_all-built databases.
4. Startup handles upgrade to head automatically from then on.
